nodes.body:
Target-device validation is complete: **72 passed, zero failures/errors/skips**. The suite covers actual 64-column/two-slot lowering, FP16/BF16 dense O/Stats replay, and ragged changed-length/fresh-binding/retained-capture behavior. Two representative cases each also pass unfiltered memcheck, racecheck and synccheck with zero errors/hazards.

GPU-tested `b3c7a7290` and current `03969e064` have identical kernel AST and identical other runtime/test files; the successor only changes comments and documentation placement. The PR description now records these results. Existing standard GPU CI is running.

@Anerudhan, the requested independent review is ready. Please also set the appropriate milestone as part of maintainer review; `merge-requirements` currently reports the missing milestone.

CI follow-up: the completed SM80/SM100/SM103 lanes each found the same five stale contract assertions: unconditional D128 TILE_N64 rejection, the old single-width domain, and a two-slot error message that now correctly reaches the TMEM fit guard.

`d1e8da516` updates these tests to the explicit native D128 narrow-tile contract and adds dense CGA1 rejection controls. The TMEM overflow, unsupported widths, quantized types and three-warp-group rejections remain. All 54 affected local metadata/table checks and scoped repository hooks pass. This commit changes tests only; the kernel/adapter code covered by the prior 72 target tests and sanitizer results is unchanged.

@cudnn-ci-bot run python/sdpa/frost

